\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \times 3^2 = \frac{9\sqrt{3}}{4}
$$

And the area of the larger triangle is:

$$
\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \times 12^2 = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \times 144 = 36\sqrt{3}
$$

